{
  "id": "BP-PLATFORM-25-designer",
  "bp_entry": "BP-PLATFORM-25",
  "title": "The designer without a browser: export and import round trip, instances, step log, DLQ retry; the checks the runner cannot do are named 'not run' with an owner",
  "description": "T-2816 (PM 25 Nov 20:15, from project/designer-uat-2026-11-25.md 'Not tested'). Runs on the platform tenant as the platform administrator with throwaway definitions uat-tmp-designer-<run_id>-<n>; only platform.validate_registration, no mail, no provisioner, no tenant. A: export a definition, import the document under a second name, compare the graph (round trip), a foreign schema marker is refused. B: the definition and instance lists answer; an instance whose start slug is too short fails in the validate step (the failure fixture needs no provisioner: the BP-PLATFORM-01 fixture of scenario E, a realm bound twice, does); the step log names the step, the dead-letter list holds it, a retry gives a second attempt. C: a company user cannot export. D1..D4 are 'not run' with an OWNER and a reason (blocked_by; a blocked step never fails the run): the Keycloak sign-in page (infra), the raw JSON view and the visual checks (the Playwright designer specs), the Guide click in each language (the vitest of the editor guide; the strings and the three guide documents are asserted by scripts/uat/tests/test_bp_platform_25.py). The cleanup retires the throwaway definitions through the product's own API: DELETE /api/v1/definitions/:id (draft: hard delete 204; active: deprecate then archive, 200; deprecated: archive, 200; archived: 409) and the same call for the three leftover definitions of the operator's walk (uat-tmp-walk-*), by id, tolerant of 404 and 409.",
  "tenant": "${tenant}",
  "inputs": [],
